<article id="post-1505" class="post-1505 page type-page status-publish hentry">
	<header class="entry-header">
		<h1 class="entry-title">speed of light</h1>			</header><!-- .entry-header -->
	<div class="entry-content">
		<h1><b>speed of light in vacuum</b></h1>
<h5><a href="https://metricsystem.net/si/defining-constants/">SI defining constant</a></h5>
<table>
<tbody>
<tr style="border-bottom:6px solid #FFFFFF">
<td style="background-color:#C6C6C6;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:120%;padding:4px 6px">Name</td>
<td style="background-color:#C6C6C6;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:120%;padding:4px 2px 4px 0;text-align:center">Symbol</td>
<td style="background-color:#E3E3E3;font-size:112%;padding:0;text-align:center" width="25%">Base units</td>
</tr>
<tr style="border:0">
<td style="background-color:#F6B08F;font-size:150%;padding:8px 6px">speed of light in vacuum</td>
<td style="background-color:#F6B08F;font-size:150%;padding:0 4px 0 0;text-align:center"><i>c</i></td>
<td style="background-color:#C6C6C6;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:120%;padding:0;text-align:center">m&nbsp;s<sup>-1</sup></td>
</tr>
<tr style="border:0;background-color:#FDEBE3">
<td colspan="3" style="padding:6px 0 6px 6px;vertical-align:top"><img style="float:right;padding:0 4px 4px 4px;width:25%" src="https://metricsystem.net/wp-content/uploads/2021/07/c0100000_1.png">The speed of light in vacuum, symbol <i>c</i>, is a fundamental physical constant. It is the speed at which all electromagnetic radiation travels in vacuum.<br />
&nbsp;<br />
The numerical value of the speed of light in vacuum, symbol <i>c</i>, is defined to be exactly 299 792 458 when expressed in the unit <a href="https://metricsystem.net/derived-units/coherent-derived-units/metre-per-second/">metre per second</a>, m&nbsp;s<sup>−1</sup>.</td>
</tr>
<tr style="border:0">
<td colspan="3" style="background-color:#F6B08F;text-align:center;padding:20px 4px 30px"><img src="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=c+%3D+299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458+%5Cmspace%7B6mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D&#038;bg=F6B08F&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=3&#038;c=20201002" srcset="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=c+%3D+299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458+%5Cmspace%7B6mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D&#038;bg=F6B08F&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=3&#038;c=20201002 1x, https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=c+%3D+299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458+%5Cmspace%7B6mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D&#038;bg=F6B08F&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=3&#038;c=20201002&#038;zoom=4.5 4x" alt="c = 299 &#92;mspace{4mu} 792 &#92;mspace{4mu} 458 &#92;mspace{6mu} &#92;text{m} &#92;mspace{4mu} &#92;text{s}^{-1}" class="latex" /></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Relativity</h3>
<p>The speed of light in vacuum is constant, regardless of the motion of the source or the inertial reference frame of the observer.</p>
<h3>Speed</h3>
<p>The speed of light in vacuum, <i>c</i>, forms the basis for the definition of the unit of speed, the <a href="https://metricsystem.net/derived-units/coherent-derived-units/metre-per-second/">metre per second</a>.</p>
<p>The fixed numerical value of the speed of light in vacuum, <i>c</i>, is defined exactly:</p>
<p style="text-align:center">
<img src="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=c+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D++&#038;bg=ffffff&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002" srcset="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=c+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D++&#038;bg=ffffff&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002 1x, https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=c+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D++&#038;bg=ffffff&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002&#038;zoom=4.5 4x" alt="c &#92;mspace{4mu} = 299 &#92;mspace{4mu} 792 &#92;mspace{4mu} 458 &#92; &#92;text{m} &#92; &#92;text{s}^{-1}  " class="latex" /></p>
<p>Inverting this relation gives an exact expression for the metre per second in terms of the speed of light in vacuum, <i>c</i>&nbsp;:</p>
<div style="text-align:center;padding:10px 4px 16px;background-color:#FDEBE3">
<img src="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=1+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B1%7D%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+c%5C%5C++&#038;bg=FDEBE3&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002" srcset="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=1+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B1%7D%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+c%5C%5C++&#038;bg=FDEBE3&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002 1x, https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=1+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bs%7D%5E%7B-1%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B1%7D%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+c%5C%5C++&#038;bg=FDEBE3&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002&#038;zoom=4.5 4x" alt="1 &#92;mspace{4mu} &#92;text{m} &#92;mspace{4mu} &#92;text{s}^{-1} &#92;mspace{4mu} = &#92;dfrac{1}{299 &#92;mspace{4mu} 792 &#92;mspace{4mu} 458} &#92;mspace{4mu} c&#92;&#92;  " class="latex" /></div>
<div style="padding:16px 0"></div>
<h3>Length or distance</h3>
<p>The speed of light in vacuum, <i>c</i>, together with the <a href="https://metricsystem.net/si/defining-constants/frequency-of-caesium-133/">hyperfine transition frequency of the caesium 133 atom</a>, Δ<i>ν</i><sub>Cs</sub>, forms the basis for the definition of the unit of length, the <a href="https://metricsystem.net/si/base-units/metre/">metre</a>.</p>
<p>The definition of the metre implies the exact relation:</p>
<p style="text-align:center">
<img src="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=%5Cdfrac%7Bc%7D%7B%5CDelta+%5Cnu+_%7BCs%7D%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D%7B9+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+192+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+631+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+770%7D+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D++&#038;bg=ffffff&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002" srcset="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=%5Cdfrac%7Bc%7D%7B%5CDelta+%5Cnu+_%7BCs%7D%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D%7B9+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+192+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+631+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+770%7D+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D++&#038;bg=ffffff&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002 1x, https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=%5Cdfrac%7Bc%7D%7B%5CDelta+%5Cnu+_%7BCs%7D%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D%7B9+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+192+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+631+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+770%7D+%5C+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D++&#038;bg=ffffff&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002&#038;zoom=4.5 4x" alt="&#92;dfrac{c}{&#92;Delta &#92;nu _{Cs}} &#92;mspace{4mu} = &#92;dfrac{299 &#92;mspace{4mu} 792 &#92;mspace{4mu} 458}{9 &#92;mspace{4mu} 192 &#92;mspace{4mu} 631 &#92;mspace{4mu} 770} &#92; &#92;text{m}  " class="latex" /></p>
<p>Inverting this relation gives an exact expression for the metre in terms of the speed of light in vacuum, <i>c</i>, and the caesium frequency, Δ<i>ν</i><sub>Cs</sub>&nbsp;:</p>
<div style="text-align:center;padding:10px 4px 16px;background-color:#FDEBE3">
<img src="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=1+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B9+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+192+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+631+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+770%7D%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D+%5Cmspace%7B6mu%7D+%5Cdfrac%7Bc%7D%7B%5CDelta+%5Cnu+_%7BCs%7D%7D++&#038;bg=FDEBE3&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002" srcset="https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=1+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B9+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+192+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+631+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+770%7D%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D+%5Cmspace%7B6mu%7D+%5Cdfrac%7Bc%7D%7B%5CDelta+%5Cnu+_%7BCs%7D%7D++&#038;bg=FDEBE3&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002 1x, https://s0.wp.com/latex.php?latex=1+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%5Ctext%7Bm%7D+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+%3D+%5Cdfrac%7B9+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+192+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+631+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+770%7D%7B299+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+792+%5Cmspace%7B4mu%7D+458%7D+%5Cmspace%7B6mu%7D+%5Cdfrac%7Bc%7D%7B%5CDelta+%5Cnu+_%7BCs%7D%7D++&#038;bg=FDEBE3&#038;fg=222222&#038;s=2&#038;c=20201002&#038;zoom=4.5 4x" alt="1 &#92;mspace{4mu} &#92;text{m} &#92;mspace{4mu} = &#92;dfrac{9 &#92;mspace{4mu} 192 &#92;mspace{4mu} 631 &#92;mspace{4mu} 770}{299 &#92;mspace{4mu} 792 &#92;mspace{4mu} 458} &#92;mspace{6mu} &#92;dfrac{c}{&#92;Delta &#92;nu _{Cs}}  " class="latex" /></div>
<div style="padding:16px 0"></div>
	</div><!-- .entry-content -->
</article><!-- #post-1505 -->

		</main><!-- #main -->
